Description: Provides scope, calibration and stability diagnostics to assess
    false discovery rate (FDR) claims in peptide and protein identification
    workflows based on target-decoy competition and related confidence
    measures. Includes the recomputed decoy ratio of the reported list,
    accepted decoy counts and local decoy support, the FDP-CV benchmark,
    threshold elasticity, posterior error probability (PEP) concordance with
    the decoys, equal-chance checks and p-value calibration, explicit
    target/decoy label-propagation rules for grouped units, picked-protein
    competition, external validation by entrapment (raw and size-corrected
    estimates, scope-discordant-set error rate), a ground-truth simulator of
    target-decoy competition, and an HTML report. Methods are described in
    Chion et al. (2026) <doi:10.64898/2026.04.16.718468>.
URL: https://github.com/Jacky11/diagFDR, https://www.biorxiv.org/content/10.64898/2026.04.16.718468
